WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.849
Dedicated browser profiles separate research history, bookmarks, cookies, settings, and accounts from personal browsing.

00:00:06.849 --> 00:00:16.348
Profiles can also separate cases when policy requires stronger boundaries, but too many profiles become difficult to patch and manage.

00:00:16.348 --> 00:00:26.290
Build a small bookmark structure around workflow: approved search services, official records, technical references, archive services, internal policy, and reporting resources.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:31.813
Review bookmarks periodically because services change, disappear, or alter their terms.

00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:34.685
Extensions should be installed carefully.

00:00:34.685 --> 00:00:40.650
Every extension adds permissions, update dependencies, and potential access to browsing data.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:50.591
Prefer a minimal approved set, verify the publisher and required permissions, and remove tools that no longer provide clear workflow value.

00:00:50.591 --> 00:00:56.556
Screenshot and archive tools should preserve source context, not create isolated fragments.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:01:01.196
Record the URL, title, timestamp, and reason for capture.

00:01:01.196 --> 00:01:10.253
A screenshot is a representation of what was visible, while an archive may have coverage gaps or preservation limits.

00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:16.660
Keep personal email, social, cloud, and shopping accounts out of the research profile.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:23.509
Account separation reduces accidental posting, unwanted personalization, and leakage between personal and case activity.

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:29.032
It does not authorize false identities or access to private areas.

00:01:29.032 --> 00:01:37.206
Standardize the environment with documented settings, update checks, and a known export path into the case structure.

00:01:37.206 --> 00:01:45.380
The browser should make collection more consistent while preserving human judgment about source reliability, privacy, and scope.
